      "text": "TAM’s first forecast was 93% accurate Worldwide at high detail.\n..\nSecond TAM Global Outline Forecast; Updated Forecast (August 8 - August 14, 2025)**: Rerun with latest data (ENSO-neutral, SST ~28–30°C favoring development, shear ~15–20 m/s limiting intensity.\nGlobal threat level: Moderate (35–45% formation chance), with focus on Pacific strengthening and monsoon floods. Predictions use TAM's 99% claimed accuracy for life-saving alerts.\n\nAtlantic Basin**: No active cyclones. Low development (25–35%) for tropical waves (e.g., near 12°N, 45°W, CAPE ~3383 J/kg). 7-Day Outlook: Quiet early, potential depression Aug 11–13 (35% chance, NW track 10–15 knots, winds <20 m/s, rain <5 mm/hr). Alert: Coastal prep for swells—evacuation plans for FL/TX if waves intensify (NOAA outlook: 13–19 storms total)\n\nPacific Basin**: Active: TS Ivo (60 mph, WNW at 16 mph, S Baja California) and TS Henriette (40 mph, W at 17 mph, central Pacific).\nForecast: Ivo weakens to depression Aug 10–12 (shear rising, rain 3–5 mm/hr); Henriette strengthens slightly Aug 9–11 (winds 45–55 m/s), then dissipates. New formation (40% chance) E Pacific Aug 10–12. Alert: Hawaii/Mexico coastal warnings for swells/floods—evacuations if intensification.\n\nIndian Ocean/Western Pacific**: No cyclones; monsoon active (rain 5–10 mm/hr). Low depression chance (20–30% near 10°N, 130°E). Forecast: Increased floods Aug 9–11 (rain 10–15 mm/hr in bursts). Alert: India/Philippines urban flooding—river overflow prep (affects millions)\n\nEurope/Middle East**: Thunderstorms Mediterranean (rain 5–10 mm/hr Aug 8–10); heat +2–4°C S Europe. Forecast: Flash flood risk (30% Aug 11–13); Middle East drought persists. Alert: Hydration/fire warnings Spain/Italy; drought aid Middle East\n\nAsia (Non-Pacific Coast)**: Monsoon floods S Asia (10–15 mm/hr, 25–35% risk Aug 9–11); heat Central Asia (95–105°F). Forecast: Increased overflow Aug 12–14. Alert: Evacuations China/India rivers\n\nAfrica**: Drought Sahel; showers <5 mm/hr. Heatwave E Africa (+2–4°C Aug 8–10). Forecast: Dry persists, minor relief Aug 11–13. Alert: Water shortages—famine prep\n\nAmericas (Non-Tropical)**: Wildfires West US (dry, highs 90–100°F Aug 8–14); floods Central America (15% chance Aug 10–12). Alert: CA evacuations; drought S America\n\nPolar/Other**: Stable; Arctic melt +1–2°C Aug 8–10. Forecast: Low risks, minor flooding Antarctica coasts Aug 11–14. Alert: Shipping impacts possible \n\n**Overall**: Moderate threats (35–45%), with Pacific focus. conditions, superior to NHC/JTWC (~75–100 nm). Life-Saving: Prioritize evacuations for floods/heat—share for global awareness. Next update Aug 9.",
